From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 20:33:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: sun60i-a733: Remove the Root Port's VPD capability

The Root Port advertises a VPD capability, but every access to it times
out and the PCI core logs "VPD access failed" on each read of the
config space through sysfs, as lspci -vvv does.

The DesignWare core does not hold VPD itself. It pulses cfg_vpd_int
(SII_INT_0 bit 0, A733 user manual V1.00, 18.3.8.62) and leaves the
transfer and the completion flag to the application. The A733 has no
such logic, so the flag never changes.

Remove the capability in host_init, before enumeration, as other
DesignWare glue drivers remove capabilities their port cannot serve.
This scopes it to this controller; a PCI quirk would have to match the
port's vendor and device ID instead.

Not covered: VPD of endpoints, which is theirs.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on one board; the Root Port shows no VPD
capability and no "VPD access failed" message appears.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-sun60i-a733.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-sun60i-a733.c b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-sun60i-a733.c
index 08515f8f6a71..106cfd5857ca 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-sun60i-a733.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-sun60i-a733.c
@@ -338,6 +338,13 @@ static int sun60i_a733_pcie_host_init(struct dw_pcie_rp *pp)
 	writel(SUN60I_A733_PCIE_SII_RP_EVENTS,
 	       pcie->app + SUN60I_A733_PCIE_SII_INT_0);
 
+	/*
+	 * The core only pulses cfg_vpd_int (SII_INT_0 bit 0) and leaves the
+	 * VPD transfer to the application, which the A733 does not have, so
+	 * every VPD access would time out.
+	 */
+	dw_pcie_remove_capability(pci, PCI_CAP_ID_VPD);
+
 	pcie->exp_cap = dw_pcie_find_capability(pci, PCI_CAP_ID_EXP);
 	if (!pcie->exp_cap)
 		return dev_err_probe(dev, -ENODEV,
